 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_pbpzze8",
   "entryDay": 41,
   "cause": "the expedition",
   "lines": [
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Franz Lee is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d41: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d41: 🕯️ Franz Lee is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d41: What Franz kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d41: \"Franz's gone.\" Mia looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Franz.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d41: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Esmeralda blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Herbal Medicine (Level 1). Willow bark = aspirin. Yarrow stops bleeding. Plantain draws out infection. The pharmacy is outside.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Reading the Land (Level 1). Eat the landscape with your eyes first: green + water + sun means food grows here. Start where those three meet.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: The Forager’s Eye (Level 1). You walk slower and see more. Food was always there; now you notice it.",
    "d41: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Franz Lee, 41 days. The mantle passes to Esmeralda Levy.",
    "d41: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Esmeralda Levy, 41 — a florist. Their hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Green Thumb, Literally.",
    "d41: The village's quarrel was with Franz — and Franz is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d41: At the grave, Irving, Xavier, Wei and 2 more speak for Esmeralda — \"Franz trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d41: The fire knew Esmeralda before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_h8npee3",
   "entryDay": 90,
   "cause": "starvation",
   "lines": [
    "d90: 📓 Codex: you've heard of Pocket Sand. Someone, somewhere, can do this. Now you know its name.",
    "d90: ◈ THE SYSTEM has been watching Ava — Strange 1. Three offers; they took Pocket Sand. Earned, chosen. (pocket_sand: villager level-up)",
    "d90: 📓 Codex: Ava chose Pocket Sand (pocket_sand) at Strange 1.",
    "d90: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Esmeralda Levy is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d90: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d90: 🕯️ Esmeralda Levy is dead — starvation. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d90: What Esmeralda kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d90: \"Esmeralda's gone.\" Xavier looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Esmeralda.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d90: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Irving blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d90: 📖 LEARNED: Reading Tracks (Level 1). Fresh tracks have sharp edges. Old tracks crumble. You can tell how recently something passed.",
    "d90: 📖 LEARNED: Soft Step (Level 1). Move through woods like weather. Less noise, fewer surprises.",
    "d90: 📖 LEARNED: Animal Behavior (Level 1). Most animals flee. Give them an escape route and they take it. Cornered animals fight.",
    "d90: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d90: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Esmeralda Levy, 90 days. The mantle passes to Irving Webb.",
    "d90: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Irving Webb, 46 — an arborist. Their hands know different work now: Beast-calm, Bird Whisperer, Turncoat, Trophy Room.",
    "d90: ◈ The System updates its file: the new bearer <redacted> \"Beastmaster of the Apex Predator.\" It had a word for this one before the Codex came.",
    "d90: The village's quarrel was with Esmeralda — and Esmeralda is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d90: You knew Esmeralda — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d90: At the grave, Chantal, Xavier, Wei and 4 more speak for Irving — \"Esmeralda trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d90: The fire knew Irving before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  }
 ],
